> Having a 'Normal' class to represent the board elements other than snake and ladder

A normal class (extending the BoardElement) can be added to represent the board cells,
using which we can replace the null check for regular cells of the board. The method
'getEndPosition()' can be overridden to return the startPosition in this class.

The disadvantage will be more mem consumption, as now only snake and ladder
classes are being init now and are assigned memory. In the case of 'Normal' class, we have
to define the object for each normal cell

> Dice with configurable counts

Approach 1 : To extend the game to have multiple dices, we can have either a variable on board which
will call the rollDice() method of the same Dice 'n' times

Approach 2 : Implement the class with diceCount

public class Dice {
    private int diceCount;
    private boolean initialized = false;

    private Dice() {}

    private static class DiceHelper {
        private static final Dice INSTANCE = new Dice();
    }

    public static Dice getInstance() {
        return DiceHelper.INSTANCE;
    }

    public synchronized void initialize(int diceCount) {
        if (initialized) {
            throw new IllegalStateException("Already initialized");
        }
        this.diceCount = diceCount;
        this.initialized = true;
    }
}

// Usage:
Dice dice = Dice.getInstance();
dice.initialize(6);
